into the cell. Complete resolution of diffusion abnormality in acute
stroke is thus uncommon, implying cellular injury. Our case
showed improvement and resolution of white matter and diffusion
abnormalities as the venous flow was restored. This reversibility
of cellular swelling may underlie the resolution of the clinical
symptoms.
